There used to be a wonderful variant scam on this: pile
everything in a corner of the shop where you'd carefully dug
diagonally adjacent holes in the two walls.  Now you could
stand "not in the shop" and kick things from "in the shop"
to "not in the shop", and the shopkeeper's sense of honor
let you get away with it, since you weren't in his/her shop
_and_ robbing it.

Over time, though, as losses mounted, the shopkeepers
started whining to the dev team about how unfair this all
was, the dev team caved under the intense pressure (and
probably massive bribes) from the Big Business interests,
and the shopkeepers got an upgrade to "walls that heal".

Politics as usual, aceing out the little guy just trying to
make a dishonest buck. Foo. Back to overfeeding worthless
